In /cost, 8 of the gemini 3.x flash models that were billed at a made-up $0.15/$0.60 now show Google's real prices. A ninth (gemini-3.6-flash) got a real price too, but it still disagrees with models.dev on purpose. The change is in commit 7971b020, with a comment on #1012. fmt, clippy with -D warnings, build and the full cargo test all pass.

Audit before and after: the live comparison against models.dev went from 53 matching and 48 drifting to 61 matching and 40 drifting. The 8 rows that dropped out are exactly the ones I fixed, and no row started drifting.

What I fixed (each price read off Google's pricing page today and agreeing with models.dev):
• gemini-3-flash-preview
• gemini-3.1-flash-lite
• gemini-3.5-flash-lite
• gemini-3.1-flash-image
• gemini-3.1-flash-lite-image
• gemini-3.1-flash-live-preview
• gemini-3.1-flash-tts-preview
• gemini-3.5-live-translate-preview

For the image, speech and live models, /cost uses the same output rate models.dev lists: the image rate for image models, the audio rate for speech, the text rate for live.

`gemini-3.6-flash` still drifts, by decision. Google charges an introductory $0.75/$3.75 until 2026-12-31, and models.dev lists that price. I used the regular $1.50/$7.50, the same rule yoagent already applies to gemini-3.8-flash. So until 2027 /cost shows about twice the actual bill for this model; before, it showed about a fifth. The docs say this.

Still guessed: gemini-3.5-flash, gemini-3.7-flash, gemini-3.1-flash-image-preview and gemini-3.1-flash-lite-preview keep the $0.15/$0.60 estimate, because Google's page doesn't list them. A test pins that they stay on the estimate.

Tests: a new test in src/format/cost/price_audit_tests.rs checks each fixed price. As a check on the test itself, I put the old guessed price back on the 3.5-flash-lite entry: the test failed and named that model, then passed again once I restored it. I also changed one existing test, test_pricing_gemini_30_flash, which had locked in the old wrong price. It now expects $0.50/$3.00.

Files: src/format/cost.rs grew by 15 lines to 3578, under its 3605 size limit. I also added the new prices to the Gemini table in docs/src/features/cost-tracking.md.

Backlog: none of the 40 rows left on #1012 needs fixing for the model picker. Three of them are in the picker, but all three disagree on purpose: one is a recorded difference and two are priced by yoagent at the regular rate. The other 37 only matter if someone types the model name. My #1012 comment names the gemini pro estimate as the next candidate. It also asks the next planner to decide whether this 37-row tail is still worth fixing row by row, or whether /cost should just label those prices as estimates.
